# NestJS Conventions

## Module structure
- One feature = one module. Modules export only what other modules need.
- `AppModule` is composition, not logic. No providers declared directly there.
- Configuration via `@nestjs/config` with a typed schema (Joi or Zod). Never read `process.env` outside config.
- `ConfigModule.forRoot({ isGlobal: true, validate })` once at the root.

## Dependency injection
- Constructor injection only. No property injection, no `Inject()` strings unless unavoidable.
- Use injection tokens (`const KAFKA_CLIENT = Symbol('KAFKA_CLIENT')`) for non-class providers.
- Custom providers (`useFactory`, `useClass`, `useValue`) live in the module that owns them.
- Singleton scope by default. `Scope.REQUEST` only when truly per-request state is needed (it disables caching and hurts perf).

## Service responsibilities (per HerdLink architecture)
- Controllers/Gateways/Resolvers are thin — parse, delegate, format. No business logic.
- Services hold logic. Pure functions where possible; side effects (DB, Kafka, Redis) at the edges.
- Repositories isolate persistence. Services depend on repository interfaces, not concrete clients.
- Kafka consumers are providers implementing `OnModuleInit` (subscribe) and `OnModuleDestroy` (commit + disconnect).

## Lifecycle hooks
- `OnModuleInit`: open connections, subscribe to topics, warm caches.
- `OnApplicationBootstrap`: cross-module readiness (e.g., geofence-engine loads fences from device-service).
- `OnModuleDestroy` / `OnApplicationShutdown`: drain consumers, commit offsets, close pools. Implement `enableShutdownHooks()` in `main.ts`.

## Validation
- `class-validator` + `class-transformer` on all DTOs.
- Global `ValidationPipe` with `whitelist: true, forbidNonWhitelisted: true, transform: true`.
- Validation errors return typed `BadRequestException` with field-level detail.

## Error handling
- Global exception filter that maps domain errors → HTTP/GraphQL/Kafka responses.
- Never leak stack traces to clients. Log full context server-side with correlation ID.
- Domain errors live in `src/errors/` and extend a base `DomainError`.

## Interceptors and pipes
- Logging interceptor: wraps every request with correlation ID, latency, status.
- Tracing interceptor: starts/ends OpenTelemetry spans with route + method as span name.
- Metrics interceptor: increments RED counters per route.
- Don't put business logic in interceptors.

## Testing
- `@nestjs/testing` `Test.createTestingModule` for unit tests.
- Override providers with mocks at the module level, not via Jest module mocking.
- Integration tests bootstrap the real module against Testcontainers (Kafka/Redis/Postgres/Mongo) — no mocks.
- E2E tests use `supertest` against a live `INestApplication`.

## GraphQL (dashboard-api)
- Code-first with `@nestjs/graphql` and `@apollo/server`. Schema generated from decorators.
- Resolvers stay thin — delegate to services.
- DataLoader for N+1 prevention on every nested field that hits a datasource.
- Federation not needed; this is a BFF.

## WebSockets (realtime-gateway)
- `@WebSocketGateway` with `socket.io` adapter.
- Authenticated connections only — verify JWT in `handleConnection`, disconnect on failure.
- Per-client room subscriptions (e.g., `farm:${farmId}`) so fan-out is scoped.

## Anti-patterns to refuse
- Logic in controllers.
- Direct `new Service()` instantiation — use DI.
- `forwardRef` to break circular deps — restructure modules instead.
- `any` in DTOs.
- Global modules for anything that isn't truly cross-cutting (config, logger, tracing).
